---
title: Mobile Offline Submission — Local Evidence and Production Boundaries
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Customer
  participant UI as React Native UI
  participant DB as SQLite + durable files
  participant S as Foreground sync engine
  participant A as Claims API
  participant PG as PostgreSQL
  participant O as Object storage
  participant W as Publisher / Queue / Worker
  participant L as Legacy claims system
  U->>UI: Start claim and select photos
  UI->>DB: Persist draft, stable clientClaimId and file records
  U->>UI: Submit while offline
  UI->>DB: Transaction: freeze payload and enqueue
  UI-->>U: Waiting to send — saved on device
  Note over DB,S: Process may terminate, no guaranteed sync while closed
  Note over UI,S: Reopen with valid session and reconnect
  S->>DB: Reset interrupted states, read due work
  S->>A: POST metadata + manifest + same clientClaimId
  A->>PG: Transaction: claim, evidence metadata, event and outbox
  PG-->>A: Commit
  alt Response arrives
    A-->>S: 201 + claimId / reference
  else Accepted response lost
    Note over S,A: Persisted backoff, replay original clientClaimId
    S->>A: POST same intake identity
    A->>PG: Customer-scoped unique identity lookup
    A-->>S: 200 + same claimId / reference
  end
  S->>DB: Persist acknowledgment before document lookup
  UI-->>U: Submitted + reference, photos pending
  loop Each incomplete attachment
    S->>A: Read claim, reconcile document completion
    alt Server already completed it
      S->>DB: Persist file completion
    else File still pending
      S->>A: Request fresh presigned PUT URL
      A-->>S: Owned object capability
      S->>O: PUT entire file with progress
      S->>A: Confirm document receipt
      A->>O: HEAD validates size / type
      A->>PG: Commit completion, release metadata readiness
      A-->>S: Receipt confirmed
      S->>DB: Persist file completion
    end
  end
  Note over PG,O: Local: not_scanned. Production: quarantine + clean verdict also required
  W->>PG: Select eligible retained outbox intent
  W->>W: Enqueue, mark publication, at-least-once delivery
  W->>L: Create with stable platform reference
  L-->>W: Legacy claim number
  W->>PG: Atomically commit delivery / number / timeline / notification
  loop Reconciliation while nonterminal
    W->>L: Poll status using verified lookup contract
    L-->>W: Last-known adjudication state
    W->>PG: Fenced lease, append changed status
  end
  UI->>A: Foreground / periodic / manual refresh
  A->>PG: Customer-scoped status timeline
  A-->>UI: Status projection and timestamps
  UI-->>U: Updated timeline
  Note over UI,L: Eventual consistency, production push is a hint, local inbox is a substitute
